32d2432f2eb9c230c8e2.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 2 at 3:29PM MST until November 6 at 12:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...The National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a Flood Warning\nfor the following rivers in Colorado...\n\nRio Grande At Alamosa affecting Alamosa County.\n\n.Minor flooding along the Rio Grande through Alamosa is expected due\nto upstream flooding occurring in the vicinity of Monte Vista.\n\nFor the Rio Grande...including Alamosa...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande at Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday afternoon to late Thursday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 9.0 feet, Minor flooding. Minor agricultural flooding\nin low lying areas along the river.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 2:30 PM MST Monday the stage was 2.7 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 7.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage early\nWednesday afternoon to a crest of 9.6 feet late Wednesday\nevening. It will then fall below flood stage early Thursday\nafternoon.\n- Flood stage is 9.0 feet.\n- http://www.water.noaa.gov","ends":"2026-11-06T00:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f77eed9d842c708a5a3d2e5d0c786d35cd12c2c0.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f77eed9d842c708a5a3d2e5d0c786d35cd12c2c0.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 2 at 12:52PM MST until November 2 at 9:30PM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"Upstream flooding along the Rio Grande continues downstream near\nMonte Vista in Rio Grande County.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding along the Rio Grande near Monte Vista is forecasted\nto begin by early afternoon on Monday.\n\n* WHERE...East Central Rio Grande County in south central Colorado...\nWest Central Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 930 PM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...The Rio Grande continues to rise due to upstream flooding\nthrough Del Norte and South Fork. Extensive inundation of low-lying\nareas adjacent to the river is expected. Inundation of low spots\nalong Highway 285, some homes, and other structures may be possible\nfor areas south of the river. Expect many areas of slow moving or\nstanding water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1251 PM MST, Upstream stream gauges on the Rio Grande and\nSouth Fork Rio Grande indicate that flooding is occurring.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMonte Vista.\n- http://water.noaa.gov","ends":"2026-11-02T21:30:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.da4d217834c7088518767dad11bd998f6f765b61.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.da4d217834c7088518767dad11bd998f6f765b61.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-02T23:20:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 022320 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 420 PM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Strong north winds and showers/isolated t-storms on the plains into this evening, perhaps some snow showers along the Palmer Divide overnight. - Generally dry and breezy on Tue, strongest winds early in the day on the plains. - Weak trough will bring scattered show","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-02T08:09:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 020809 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 109 AM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-030815- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mosqu","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB"